<title>ISRAEL: Israel govt to sell off Loram development firm.</title>
<headline>Israel govt to sell off Loram development firm.</headline>
<dateline>JERUSALEM 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The ministerial privatisation committee approved on Monday a proposal by the Government Corporations Authority to sell off the Israeli government's holdings in Loram, the Lod-Ramle development company.</p>
<p>The government holds 95 percent of Loram, a real estate developer in the Lod-Ramle area, near Ben-Gurion airport. The shares will be sold to private investors, the prime minister's office said.</p>
<p>-Jerusalem newsroom, 972-2-537-0502</p>
